{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>He sits in ambush</b> — every ambusher sits in a place where there is no settlement, but this one ambushes in a settlement." "<b>for the unfortunate</b> — Some say that the kaf is in place of the word 'like.' One may rebut them regarding the missing yod, for when 'house,' 'olive,' and 'night' are in construct state, the yod does not disappear. Now in חלכאים there is a disagreement between ketiv and qeri, whether it is one word or two, and the meaning of כאים is like נכאים, on the pattern of דוים, plural." "And a great grammarian said: חלכאים is one word, and it is from the quadriliteral forms." "And the word לחלכה is like it, and the heh is in place of alef. The Gaon [Saadia] said: the nun of יצפנו is added, and its meaning is 'he will lie in wait,' and the proof is 'his eyes,' like 'his eyes will secretly watch among the nations' (תצפנה). And what is correct in my eyes: that he lies in wait for their souls, and the meaning is that his eyes seek a hidden and concealed place."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:56.540516333Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}